WEBVTT

00:39.539 --> 00:43.084
Now, the young master is at Songrim,
this room will be vacant for a while.

00:43.168 --> 00:45.962
Put away his books, clothes,
and all his other belongings.

00:46.046 --> 00:47.005
- Yes, ma'am.
- Go ahead.

00:49.841 --> 00:54.054
He's left to train before, 12 times,
and all 12 times he was sent back.

00:54.637 --> 00:57.098
Shouldn't we wait a few days
in case he comes back again?

00:57.932 --> 00:59.184
This time will be different.

00:59.976 --> 01:02.896
Our young master has really changed.

01:04.189 --> 01:07.025
This room may soon
belong to a married couple.

01:07.108 --> 01:08.777
That's why we're cleaning.

01:08.860 --> 01:10.945
Is the young master promised
to another lady?

01:12.489 --> 01:16.326
If he calls it off again,
it will be hard for him to ever marry.

01:16.409 --> 01:17.911
It's different this time.

01:17.994 --> 01:21.664
There's a young lady
our young master's quite taken with.

01:21.748 --> 01:22.874
He's in love.

01:23.666 --> 01:25.502
- I see.
- Right, Mu-deok?

01:27.253 --> 01:29.798
You know what I mean. His bird's egg.

01:30.799 --> 01:34.844
I've been thinking
and I'm certain it's the lady in Songrim.

01:35.845 --> 01:38.306
Bird's egg at the very top of a tall tree

01:38.389 --> 01:40.934
sounds like she's aloof.

01:41.518 --> 01:43.311
And he feels protective.

01:43.394 --> 01:46.106
The kind of girl
who is like a white heron.

01:46.189 --> 01:47.232
Like me.

01:47.315 --> 01:48.608
I'm not sure.

01:49.359 --> 01:52.612
When that bird's egg of his
actually hatches,

01:52.695 --> 01:55.615
it may turn out to be
a vicious eagle, not a heron.

01:56.908 --> 01:57.742
You think so?

01:58.743 --> 02:00.286
An eagle would be frightening.

02:01.121 --> 02:03.498
Even a woodpecker or cuckoo would be bad.

02:03.581 --> 02:05.166
There's no use in worrying.

02:05.750 --> 02:08.753
I'm sure when the egg hatches,
it will just fly away.

02:10.338 --> 02:13.424
How could she do that when she loves him?

02:14.717 --> 02:19.389
If they're so close to each other,
he won't be the only one in love.

02:20.306 --> 02:22.433
The bird's egg would have felt the same.

02:23.768 --> 02:24.811
Ah!

02:25.311 --> 02:27.438
I really do hope it's Young Lady Heo.

02:28.314 --> 02:29.858
She does look like his mother.

02:32.485 --> 02:33.319
Oh, Mr. Lee.

02:34.028 --> 02:36.823
Do not touch those.
They belong to Master Jang Gang.

02:37.740 --> 02:38.908
All right. Hurry up.

02:43.204 --> 02:45.331
The things Jang Uk and I shared

02:46.457 --> 02:48.585
were a desperation to survive…

02:51.963 --> 02:54.465
and earnest desire to find ourselves…

03:04.184 --> 03:05.685
and a firm promise

03:07.395 --> 03:10.648
that we would part ways
as soon as we got what we wanted.

03:12.650 --> 03:15.320
Even if the affection
Maidservant Kim speaks of…

03:17.363 --> 03:19.574
…is lingering somewhere between us,

03:20.867 --> 03:25.955
it is nothing but a shell
to be discarded once the egg hatches.

03:47.685 --> 03:50.980
Did you really memorize all this already?

03:51.064 --> 03:53.024
Yes, and you can check
each and every word.

03:53.691 --> 03:54.859
I didn't miss a single letter.

03:57.904 --> 03:58.947
But still,

03:59.030 --> 04:01.282
even if you're quick,
this should at least take a month.

04:01.366 --> 04:03.034
I've had 12 masters in the past

04:03.117 --> 04:05.787
which means I've read
the same books 12 times already.

04:05.870 --> 04:09.332
This is like a total piece of cake for me
at least. Something like that, yeah.

04:09.415 --> 04:12.752
I knew it. I knew it. I wondered
why he was following the rules.

04:12.835 --> 04:14.379
He had his reasons.

04:14.462 --> 04:17.882
So now that I'm free to come and go,
I'm going back home now.

04:18.383 --> 04:19.550
You may not leave yet.

04:27.517 --> 04:28.601
Why can't I leave yet?

04:29.185 --> 04:31.187
According to the rules,
since I've mastered the basics,

04:31.271 --> 04:32.313
I should be allowed to go.

04:32.397 --> 04:34.565
The reason I told you to read this book

04:34.649 --> 04:36.693
was to have it engraved
deeply in your heart,

04:36.776 --> 04:38.695
not just for you to memorize it.

04:39.445 --> 04:41.823
However, since you are
sly enough to deceive us,

04:41.906 --> 04:45.201
I don't believe that you've truly mastered
this learning at all.

04:46.786 --> 04:48.204
So, it seems to me that

04:48.913 --> 04:51.791
Songrim's leader can change
the regulations whenever he likes.

04:53.251 --> 04:54.085
For you.

04:54.794 --> 04:56.713
It will be another piece of cake.

04:57.297 --> 04:59.507
I'll allow you to come and go as you like

05:01.217 --> 05:04.178
just as soon as you finish
reading this book.

05:16.524 --> 05:18.401
So, I will actually be allowed to leave

05:19.652 --> 05:21.112
if I just read one book?

05:21.195 --> 05:22.155
That's right.

05:23.031 --> 05:25.825
Go read this book. It should be…

05:26.659 --> 05:29.245
just as easy as eating a piece of cake.

05:30.038 --> 05:31.789
Oh, dear!

05:32.457 --> 05:34.292
Mu-deok won't be seeing Uk for a while.

05:48.514 --> 05:50.099
Wait. This book is blank?

05:52.518 --> 05:56.564
It's not blank. There are… words there.

05:57.815 --> 05:58.816
Come on, there's nothing.

05:58.900 --> 06:01.110
You're saying you can read this?

06:01.778 --> 06:03.237
It's just that you can't see it.

06:04.155 --> 06:06.699
It's Words of the Heart,
by Master Seo Gyeong.

06:06.783 --> 06:09.285
It can only be read
if you focus all your energy.

06:12.997 --> 06:13.831
Hmm.

06:14.916 --> 06:17.418
So you're supposed to see something here?

06:18.044 --> 06:20.546
And I apparently
just can't see it, I guess.

06:26.010 --> 06:27.637
Hey, Dang-gu, I heard your friend

06:27.720 --> 06:29.472
didn't even know Words of the Heart.

06:29.555 --> 06:33.101
He's never even had proper training.
Of course, he wouldn't know.

06:33.184 --> 06:37.230
He can't leave the Training Center
until he finishes reading that book.

06:37.313 --> 06:38.398
What will he do?

06:38.481 --> 06:40.441
He will be in there
for at least six months then?

06:41.484 --> 06:43.903
With his skills,
how could he do it in six months?

06:43.986 --> 06:45.988
He might have mastered Ryusu
through pure luck,

06:46.072 --> 06:47.448
but he hasn't been properly trained.

06:48.616 --> 06:50.451
I bet it'll take him over a year.

06:59.877 --> 07:02.505
How would you know
if you've never even read it yourselves?

07:02.588 --> 07:05.466
At least, I know how much training
you need in order to read it.

07:05.550 --> 07:08.052
Then you should also know
just how far ahead of you he is.

07:08.845 --> 07:10.096
Since you haven't received it…

07:11.305 --> 07:12.682
and yet Uk already has.

07:17.812 --> 07:20.565
He's right, guys. You guys shouldn't talk
about things you don't understand.

07:20.648 --> 07:21.482
See ya.

07:23.526 --> 07:24.569
Damn it.

07:29.615 --> 07:31.993
Why do you think Uncle
already gave Uk Words of the Heart?

07:32.827 --> 07:34.495
I don't know.

07:35.079 --> 07:37.248
As long as he's busy with that,
he can't do anything.

07:37.790 --> 07:38.833
And he's stuck here.

07:45.673 --> 07:46.507
Well…

07:47.675 --> 07:49.719
I have no intentions of training Jang Uk.

07:50.344 --> 07:54.432
He'll be under my watch, so at least
he won't be able to wander around

07:55.308 --> 07:56.601
causing trouble.

07:56.684 --> 07:59.645
So you didn't accept him into Songrim,

07:59.729 --> 08:01.606
you merely trapped him inside it.

08:03.232 --> 08:05.651
Since we've made
such a show of accepting Uk,

08:06.360 --> 08:07.904
I'm sure his father will come.

08:07.987 --> 08:10.072
By "his father", you mean Jang Gang?

08:10.156 --> 08:12.617
The opening of his son's gate of energy…

08:14.744 --> 08:17.371
was the one thing
Jang Gang feared the most.

08:17.955 --> 08:19.207
If he catches wind of this,

08:20.249 --> 08:22.126
he is certain to come back.

08:22.210 --> 08:23.711
If we're gonna get rid of Jin Mu,

08:24.212 --> 08:26.714
then we will definitely need
the Gwanju to return.

08:27.882 --> 08:29.342
Jang Gang must return…

08:31.177 --> 08:33.221
for all of our problems to be solved.

08:34.972 --> 08:37.099
Anyway, I do take pity on our Uk.

08:37.892 --> 08:39.810
He's already come this far without

08:39.894 --> 08:42.146
any proper training.

08:42.230 --> 08:43.606
But reading that book?

08:43.689 --> 08:45.525
Impossible.

08:53.449 --> 08:55.743
Why have you prepared
these snacks for him?

08:56.827 --> 08:58.788
I've heard some things
about that Young Master Jang.

08:58.871 --> 09:01.165
He has a complicated family history,

09:01.249 --> 09:03.543
- and he's weak and hot-tempered.
- He's not.

09:05.878 --> 09:06.921
He's a good man.

09:07.004 --> 09:08.673
Okay. How do you know?

09:09.173 --> 09:10.716
I heard he's so difficult

09:10.800 --> 09:14.011
that his servant, Mu-deok, is the only one
who can possibly put up with him.

09:16.264 --> 09:17.807
- Mu-deok?
- Yes.

09:17.890 --> 09:20.851
The girl servant that
Young Master Jang keeps by his side.

09:20.935 --> 09:21.769
That Mu-deok.

09:26.023 --> 09:26.983
Hey, Mu-deok.

09:27.858 --> 09:30.528
I heard that you stayed
right by my side the whole night.

09:30.611 --> 09:33.739
I thought you were my servant, Mu-deok.
I apologize for my rudeness.

09:35.324 --> 09:37.827
So, that's why he thought
I was Mu-deok that night.

09:39.078 --> 09:39.912
Hmm.

09:44.125 --> 09:45.001
Good day.

09:47.420 --> 09:48.838
We are both from Sejukwon.

09:49.714 --> 09:50.673
Let's go, my lady.

10:29.170 --> 10:31.422
Uh, but the fire…

10:57.782 --> 10:58.741
For you.

10:58.824 --> 11:00.451
It will be another piece of cake.

11:05.915 --> 11:07.124
I've been fooled.

11:07.208 --> 11:09.126
Ugh, I can't believe
he tricked me like that.

11:26.310 --> 11:28.145
Uh, we meet again.

11:28.229 --> 11:31.982
Uh, yeah. Are you going somewhere?

11:32.066 --> 11:34.443
Ugh, yeah. There's someone I need to meet.

11:35.861 --> 11:38.489
But why are you going this way?

11:38.572 --> 11:39.407
Uh…

11:40.157 --> 11:41.242
because I am running away.

11:41.826 --> 11:43.202
Ah.

11:43.285 --> 11:46.038
So… pretend you didn't see this, either.

11:47.081 --> 11:48.332
Oh!

11:49.709 --> 11:51.752
My gosh.
Young Lady Heo is so impatient.

11:51.836 --> 11:53.838
Honestly. Why did she not wait for me?

11:53.921 --> 11:55.923
I can't believe she left me behind.

12:00.970 --> 12:01.846
What's the matter?

12:02.346 --> 12:03.180
Huh!

12:03.889 --> 12:05.433
Is Uk not in his room right now?

12:06.016 --> 12:07.601
Oh, no. He's in there.

12:08.310 --> 12:09.562
Then, let's go.

12:09.645 --> 12:13.357
But I… have something to discuss
with Young Master Jang.

12:13.441 --> 12:15.151
I'd like to be alone with him now.

12:17.653 --> 12:20.823
And I think it'll take quite a while,
so wait for me outside.

12:40.718 --> 12:43.637
Hey, Mu-deok,
a young man has come from Songrim.

12:43.721 --> 12:45.097
He's looking for you.

13:02.907 --> 13:04.575
Hello, Young Master Seo.

13:07.244 --> 13:08.871
I guess you must have thought I was Uk.

13:10.831 --> 13:12.666
You probably won't see him for a while.

13:13.751 --> 13:15.586
He has a rather
difficult task to complete.

13:16.337 --> 13:17.797
I'm sure he'll do well.

13:18.714 --> 13:20.800
For now, what's most important for him

13:21.383 --> 13:23.886
is just to stay there and get stronger.

13:24.637 --> 13:27.640
I was worried after you left,
but you seem to be all right.

13:28.682 --> 13:30.559
So, what are you doing
these days without Uk?

13:31.352 --> 13:35.022
I'm a servant,
so my job is to do chores all day.

13:35.898 --> 13:39.610
Maidservant Kim isn't here right now.
So will you wait for her in the study?

13:40.194 --> 13:41.946
I'm not here to see her. I'm here for you.

13:44.073 --> 13:44.990
To see me?

13:46.116 --> 13:48.369
But what business could you
possibly have with me?

13:49.203 --> 13:50.037
Uh…

13:50.871 --> 13:52.081
you have…

13:52.998 --> 13:56.752
my umbrella that I lent you.

13:58.170 --> 13:59.505
Oh, that.

13:59.588 --> 14:02.383
I threw it out
because it ripped on my way back here.

14:03.801 --> 14:04.677
Really?

14:07.096 --> 14:08.055
Then let's go out.

14:08.764 --> 14:09.598
What?

14:09.682 --> 14:10.683
I need a new umbrella.

14:11.350 --> 14:13.978
I want you to buy it.

14:16.605 --> 14:19.400
UMBRELLAS

14:22.653 --> 14:25.489
This one looks exactly like
the umbrella you lent me.

14:25.573 --> 14:26.866
This is made with very…

14:28.909 --> 14:30.578
very low-quality paper.

14:31.245 --> 14:33.414
Mine was made with sheepskin and bamboo.

14:35.082 --> 14:36.417
How nice!

14:37.126 --> 14:39.420
Why did you give
such a nice umbrella to a servant?

14:39.503 --> 14:41.422
I didn't give it. It was a loan.

14:41.505 --> 14:44.258
If you lose someone's belonging,
you should pay for a new one.

14:46.385 --> 14:48.637
And anyway, that was
the only umbrella I had.

14:48.721 --> 14:51.849
Why would the young master
of the Seo family have only one umbrella?

14:51.932 --> 14:53.976
I usually don't go outside when it rains.

14:55.269 --> 14:59.189
My injury from when I was young,
it aches more when it's raining.

15:00.441 --> 15:03.485
The leg you broke,
it still hurts sometimes?

15:07.740 --> 15:10.659
I heard from Young Master Park
that you broke your leg once.

15:12.077 --> 15:13.913
I was injured in Danhyanggok.

15:13.996 --> 15:17.458
How sad that you draw energy
from water but hurt when it rains.

15:18.459 --> 15:20.336
Your leg must not have healed properly.

15:23.255 --> 15:24.214
I had a friend

15:25.507 --> 15:27.301
who had waited for me in Danhyanggok.

15:30.304 --> 15:32.222
She saved me and treated my wound.

15:33.766 --> 15:36.018
It must not have fully healed
because we parted ways…

15:37.561 --> 15:38.896
before I could thank her.

15:52.660 --> 15:54.662
- I like this one.
- What?

15:54.745 --> 15:56.830
I want this one. Go pay for it.

15:58.958 --> 15:59.792
Yes.

16:05.089 --> 16:06.548
- This one, please.
- Of course.

16:06.632 --> 16:09.093
Put it on Master Jang Gang's tab, please.

16:09.677 --> 16:12.554
Why are you putting it on Uk's tab?
You should pay for it.

16:13.180 --> 16:15.599
Gosh, how would a servant like me
have any money?

16:15.683 --> 16:16.850
I know you should have some.

16:17.434 --> 16:19.061
I saw you spending the money you hid

16:19.144 --> 16:21.438
to enjoy yourself and buy nice clothes.

16:21.522 --> 16:22.982
I wasn't that…

16:27.778 --> 16:30.614
- How much?
- You must have a good eye.

16:30.698 --> 16:33.492
You selected the most
expensive one I have.

16:45.087 --> 16:46.296
Mu-deok isn't here?

16:47.464 --> 16:50.342
Where could she have gone
just when I needed her, huh?

16:50.426 --> 16:52.928
Young Master, did you get
kicked out of training again?

16:53.512 --> 16:56.015
I did not! I'm only
just out for a little bit.

16:56.098 --> 16:57.933
And I'm going back soon, okay?

16:58.017 --> 16:58.851
Ah.

16:58.934 --> 17:00.769
Mu-deok will be back soon as well.

17:01.353 --> 17:03.814
Would you like to take
a hot bath while you wait?

17:04.523 --> 17:05.441
Could I?

17:05.524 --> 17:07.943
It's been quite a while
since I last took a bath at my house.

17:08.027 --> 17:09.945
- I'll go get it ready then.
- Hmm.

17:14.491 --> 17:15.325
Hmm?

17:26.211 --> 17:27.129
Oh.

17:28.630 --> 17:30.674
Were our honey biscuits always this sweet?

17:33.052 --> 17:35.429
Why are there no snacks in Songrim?

17:36.013 --> 17:38.140
Even the leader used to have
a sweet tooth.

17:38.807 --> 17:39.641
Hmm.

17:55.324 --> 17:56.575
Are we here today…

17:57.785 --> 17:59.244
so that you can break up with me?

18:00.162 --> 18:01.580
Yes.

18:02.164 --> 18:05.209
In just a bit, the three
gossiping girls will walk by

18:05.292 --> 18:06.502
after floriculture class.

18:06.585 --> 18:09.296
If they see the two of us
fighting when they get here,

18:09.379 --> 18:12.091
they'll spread the rumor of our breakup
everywhere in no time.

18:17.971 --> 18:18.889
As promised,

18:19.640 --> 18:22.059
let's stage it so it looks like my fault.

18:22.684 --> 18:25.062
First, slap me across the face.

18:25.145 --> 18:27.981
Then, when I cling to you, push me away
and storm out through that door.

18:28.065 --> 18:30.609
But that seems a bit extreme.

18:30.692 --> 18:32.402
It has to be
to call off a marriage.

18:32.486 --> 18:34.488
We'll need to show
all of them quite a scene.

18:34.571 --> 18:35.489
Make it real.

18:35.572 --> 18:39.076
If we do that, awful rumors
will spread about you, Dang-gu.

18:39.159 --> 18:42.663
If you ruin your reputation,
there'll be no matchmaking for you.

18:45.582 --> 18:46.458
I don't…

18:47.459 --> 18:49.503
want to get married by matchmaking.

18:53.132 --> 18:54.716
I want to marry someone…

18:56.009 --> 18:57.136
for love

19:05.894 --> 19:07.229
Slapping is too much, though.

19:08.605 --> 19:11.191
I'll just… throw this at you.

19:11.775 --> 19:14.695
Oh, yeah. Let's do that way, then.

19:18.240 --> 19:19.658
This tea is too hot.

19:20.826 --> 19:22.828
You'll get burnt if I throw it.

19:28.292 --> 19:29.585
Oh! Goodness.

19:30.711 --> 19:31.837
I'll be fine.

19:33.922 --> 19:37.342
I heard people say that
there's a magic show in a few days.

19:39.052 --> 19:40.637
I really want to see it.

19:41.471 --> 19:44.391
But if I break up with you,
I guess I won't be able to.

19:45.017 --> 19:47.269
What? Why?

19:47.352 --> 19:51.190
In my experience,
if you ever call off a wedding,

19:52.107 --> 19:55.027
you're expected to
remain at home for a month at least.

19:55.944 --> 19:57.821
Oh, I see.

20:02.034 --> 20:06.205
All right, well, uh, should we delay
breaking up a few days?

20:06.288 --> 20:07.122
Could we?

20:09.249 --> 20:13.337
Uh, but my-my friends will also be there.

20:14.171 --> 20:17.591
So I don't want to go by myself.

20:17.674 --> 20:22.262
Uh, well, since we are still a couple,
then we should go together.

20:24.514 --> 20:27.267
Well, if you insist.

20:31.855 --> 20:34.608
I'll take the pumpkin taffy,

20:34.691 --> 20:36.735
rice taffy, and honey biscuits.

20:36.818 --> 20:37.653
Of course.

20:39.613 --> 20:41.281
The young master is a picky eater,

20:41.782 --> 20:43.909
so he gets cranky if there are no snacks.

20:44.826 --> 20:46.036
Please give these to him.

20:49.039 --> 20:50.874
I like these pine pollen tea snacks.

20:51.416 --> 20:54.044
Of course, you have expensive taste.

20:54.127 --> 20:56.505
- Would you like some of those?
- No.

21:07.808 --> 21:09.977
RECRUITING SERVANTS FOR SONGRIM

21:11.979 --> 21:13.397
RECRUITING SERVANTS FOR SONGRIM

21:13.480 --> 21:16.441
QUALIFICATIONS: HEALTHY, LITERATE,
CAN CALCULATE, NO CRIMINAL RECORD

21:18.902 --> 21:20.779
I'll put this
on the Jang family's tab.

21:27.452 --> 21:29.121
Please, give this to the young master.

21:29.746 --> 21:33.375
I have some other business
to take care of. Goodbye.

21:52.060 --> 21:53.478
- Yes, ma'am.
- Thank you.

21:54.271 --> 21:55.397
- Excuse me.
- Yes, ma'am?

21:55.480 --> 21:56.606
See you later.

22:01.737 --> 22:03.155
It is her, right?

22:03.989 --> 22:05.157
Yes, it is her.

22:06.992 --> 22:10.412
- Hey! You stole my purse, didn't you?
- Give me my ring back.

22:15.959 --> 22:16.918
Where did she go?

22:17.002 --> 22:19.463
- Hey! Hey! Stop her!
- How dare you!

22:19.546 --> 22:20.714
Stop right there!

22:22.049 --> 22:23.091
Stop that thief!

22:23.175 --> 22:25.552
- Stop!
- Get back here!

22:25.635 --> 22:28.638
Wait until I get my hands on you!

22:28.722 --> 22:30.682
Hey! Hey! Stop! You come back here.

22:31.641 --> 22:33.727
- Hey!
- What's happening here? Hey, hey!

22:33.810 --> 22:35.062
What are you doing?

22:36.772 --> 22:37.856
Catch that thief!

22:37.939 --> 22:40.108
Oh! The path is blocked! What do we do?

22:40.192 --> 22:42.402
- Hey, that's her, right?
- Yeah, yeah.

22:49.910 --> 22:50.911
That's Mu-deok.

22:51.453 --> 22:52.287
Mu-deok!

22:57.793 --> 22:59.378
- You!
- There you are, you…

22:59.461 --> 23:01.129
- Hey! Catch that thief!
- Come here!

23:01.213 --> 23:03.673
- Come here.
- Hey, stop right there.

23:04.424 --> 23:06.510
Hey! Come here, come here…

23:19.189 --> 23:20.565
It was definitely her.

23:22.442 --> 23:24.277
But how is she able to see, though?

23:38.083 --> 23:40.377
She used to always wear this
because she couldn't see.

23:42.671 --> 23:43.797
Was it not her?

24:03.733 --> 24:05.444
Well, well, I finally found you.

24:06.486 --> 24:07.529
So-i.

24:08.113 --> 24:11.116
I went all the way to Sari Village
because we'd heard you were hiding there.

24:11.199 --> 24:12.826
But you were already gone.

24:13.452 --> 24:15.662
Did you think I wouldn't be able
to find you in the capital?

24:17.456 --> 24:18.373
What's this?

24:19.916 --> 24:23.336
Don't tell me you were pretending
to be blind this time.

24:25.630 --> 24:28.133
You were always good at
putting up a pitiful front.

24:28.216 --> 24:31.553
But your real specialty is
stabbing people in their back.

24:36.683 --> 24:38.477
How dare you steal money from me?

24:40.562 --> 24:42.022
I don't know what you are talking about.

24:46.818 --> 24:48.653
Look at you trying to play me again.

24:50.697 --> 24:51.573
Go.

24:56.119 --> 24:57.329
Help me!

24:57.412 --> 24:59.080
Somebody help me!

25:01.416 --> 25:03.668
Somebody help me! I'm blind! I can't see.

25:03.752 --> 25:05.462
- Oh, dear!
- I don't know any of them,

25:06.213 --> 25:09.341
but these strange men are trying
to kidnap me! Please!

25:09.966 --> 25:12.928
Someone, anyone, help me!

25:13.011 --> 25:15.597
Look at you trying real hard.

25:17.974 --> 25:18.975
Help me!

25:19.059 --> 25:20.810
What are you all
looking at, huh?

25:21.394 --> 25:23.313
Come here.

25:33.990 --> 25:36.535
You cannot drag people off
against their will.

25:37.661 --> 25:39.871
I have a good reason
for doing this,

25:40.413 --> 25:41.873
so just be on your way.

25:42.582 --> 25:44.417
Please, sir! I cannot see anything.

25:44.501 --> 25:46.461
- And I don't even know who they are.
- You little--

25:49.089 --> 25:50.340
Get him!

26:02.435 --> 26:04.145
He's… he's a mage.

26:04.229 --> 26:05.063
Run!

26:13.655 --> 26:15.031
Are you able to stand?

26:20.287 --> 26:21.830
Thank you very much, sir.

26:21.913 --> 26:23.290
They look like dangerous men.

26:23.790 --> 26:26.001
You should properly go report it
to the authorities and get help.

26:26.876 --> 26:27.752
I'll take you.

26:27.836 --> 26:30.630
I'm all right. I don't need them.

26:32.424 --> 26:33.800
Your cane is broken.

26:40.432 --> 26:41.391
It's an umbrella.

26:42.434 --> 26:43.727
You can take this instead.

27:00.660 --> 27:03.246
Excuse me, sir, best to let her be.

27:03.330 --> 27:05.874
She refused to let you
take her to the authorities.

27:05.957 --> 27:08.251
I don't know her situation, young man,

27:08.335 --> 27:10.086
but I do know those guys were thugs.

27:10.754 --> 27:12.839
No good will come
out of involving yourself

27:12.922 --> 27:14.132
in their affairs.

27:24.643 --> 27:25.685
I'll take you.

27:26.561 --> 27:28.980
You should properly go report it
to the authorities and get help.

27:33.276 --> 27:35.028
Maybe I should have said yes then.

27:56.174 --> 27:59.177
Number 125.

28:00.261 --> 28:02.764
Is this the number of people
who have already applied?

28:02.847 --> 28:04.182
ONE HUNDRED TWENTY-FIVE

28:05.308 --> 28:07.060
And they're only going to hire five.

28:08.395 --> 28:09.979
Do I have a chance?

28:10.980 --> 28:11.815
Hey, Mu-deok.

28:13.900 --> 28:14.943
Oh, here you are.

28:15.026 --> 28:16.486
The young master's looking for you.

28:16.569 --> 28:19.030
Young Master Seo came by again?

28:19.114 --> 28:21.199
Not him. Young Master Jang Uk.

28:21.950 --> 28:24.869
Young Master Jang snuck
out of Songrim to come back home.

28:34.170 --> 28:37.048
Huh, I need to be back before sundown.
Where could she be?

29:20.341 --> 29:21.468
Where is he?

29:21.551 --> 29:23.720
He just left. I didn't see him, either.

29:26.347 --> 29:28.892
He said he'd be obedient, but he ran away.

29:30.185 --> 29:31.978
I hope he got back without getting caught.

29:35.064 --> 29:36.107
He was just here.

29:36.983 --> 29:37.984
Just now.

29:39.986 --> 29:41.696
What is with that girl?

30:06.179 --> 30:07.013
Jang Uk.

30:07.931 --> 30:08.848
Look, Young Master!

30:13.603 --> 30:16.356
Where have you been?
I thought I couldn't see you.

30:45.468 --> 30:47.804
But now, I've seen you. I'm very glad.

30:50.390 --> 30:52.851
I have to go back now,
or I'll get in trouble.

30:53.768 --> 30:56.396
Just wait there. I'll be there soon, too.

30:58.064 --> 30:59.107
I found a way.

30:59.190 --> 31:02.277
Could you stay focused
on what you need to do in there?

31:02.360 --> 31:04.070
And I'll do everything I can out here.

31:05.488 --> 31:08.116
All right. But what's the way, though?

31:09.576 --> 31:11.411
I heard Songrim is hiring servants.

31:32.098 --> 31:33.308
Be safe. Don't get caught.

31:59.334 --> 32:02.545
Your Highness,
instead of going to Sejukwon yourself,

32:02.629 --> 32:05.214
you should summon
Master Heo to the palace.

32:06.132 --> 32:09.010
That's all right.
It gives me a reason to get out.

32:09.510 --> 32:10.970
It helps my recovery.

32:17.060 --> 32:18.102
Is that Jang Uk?

32:28.404 --> 32:29.906
What are you doing out here?

32:29.989 --> 32:31.866
I heard you weren't allowed
to leave the Training Center

32:31.950 --> 32:33.868
until you're able to read
The Words of the Heart.

32:33.952 --> 32:36.371
Last time, you followed me
to where I was drinking.

32:36.454 --> 32:38.706
And now it looks like
you're keeping tabs on me.

32:38.790 --> 32:40.333
Why do you seem so interested in me?

32:40.416 --> 32:42.001
It makes me uncomfortable.

32:42.085 --> 32:44.087
Master Heo from Sejukwon told me about it.

32:45.046 --> 32:48.675
Right. I heard you fell ill
from drinking the liquor I gave you.

32:48.758 --> 32:51.052
Why did you come all the way
to Sejukwon, Your Highness?

32:51.761 --> 32:54.722
Wait, don't tell me it still hurts.

32:55.223 --> 32:57.433
Are you still in pain
from where I hit you? Oh, my goodness.

32:57.517 --> 33:00.228
No, not at all. I'm completely fine now.

33:00.728 --> 33:02.897
I just go there to get
some supplements. That's all.

33:02.981 --> 33:03.856
Hmm.

33:03.940 --> 33:05.733
I hope you take
many good supplements, sire.

33:05.817 --> 33:07.402
You must live a long, healthy life.

33:09.487 --> 33:12.073
Wait! What were you
trying to hide over there?

33:13.324 --> 33:14.242
Let me see it.

33:31.884 --> 33:32.927
It's a honey biscuit.

33:33.845 --> 33:36.180
I wanted to eat it myself.
How did you know I had it on me?

33:36.764 --> 33:37.640
You can have it.

33:44.230 --> 33:47.316
Songrim doesn't have
these kinds of snacks.

33:48.901 --> 33:49.902
Did you go home?

33:56.826 --> 33:59.954
You know you'll be in trouble
if anyone finds out you ran back home.

34:00.580 --> 34:03.833
You gave me a drink as congratulations
and even complimented me last time.

34:03.916 --> 34:06.878
Would you r-really tattle on me now
for sneaking out?

34:10.506 --> 34:12.925
I… gave you my honey biscuit.

34:18.264 --> 34:22.643
Well, stay away from that big pine tree.
I saw some mages there.

34:25.605 --> 34:27.732
Thank you very much, Your Highness.
All the best for you.

34:32.028 --> 34:33.780
I don't understand why I'm so nice to him.

34:38.618 --> 34:39.744
This is delicious.

34:40.870 --> 34:41.704
Is it really?

34:46.125 --> 34:47.085
Is it tasty?

34:48.503 --> 34:50.463
I thought that the Crown Prince

34:51.339 --> 34:53.966
would be more hostile
to Songrim after the match.

34:55.218 --> 34:57.011
Instead, he sheathed his sword

34:57.804 --> 34:59.972
and become even closer to them.

35:00.598 --> 35:03.851
He must have decided to befriend them
so they could be useful

35:03.935 --> 35:05.561
when he becomes the next king.

35:07.271 --> 35:10.650
Are you certain we shouldn't step in?

35:10.733 --> 35:11.984
Do not worry.

35:12.068 --> 35:14.028
We can change his mind quite easily.

35:14.654 --> 35:16.989
After all, we do have
Jang Uk's constellation plate.

35:18.783 --> 35:21.994
The Crown Prince will have no choice
but to kill him eventually.

35:33.214 --> 35:37.802
Is that it? This is what
we'll use to subdue Jin Ho-gyeong?

35:37.885 --> 35:41.222
The power of Jinyowon
will finally be within our grasp.

36:01.868 --> 36:04.412
It's been nearly four hours
since Young Lady Heo went inside.

36:05.830 --> 36:07.081
Oh!

36:07.165 --> 36:08.416
Don't bother them.

36:08.499 --> 36:09.834
They have a lot to talk about.

36:13.004 --> 36:16.340
Oh! Hey! Hey! Hey, wait! Stop!

36:17.633 --> 36:19.594
You really shouldn't bother them.

36:19.677 --> 36:20.845
Something's wrong.

36:20.928 --> 36:23.139
I should see whether
Jang Uk's really in there.

36:23.222 --> 36:25.433
Are you seriously doubting
what my lady said?

36:27.351 --> 36:28.352
Oh…

36:31.022 --> 36:32.565
Why isn't he back yet?

36:34.775 --> 36:38.321
If they find out he is gone,
it'll be so embarrassing.

36:48.331 --> 36:50.208
What are you doing here?
I thought you'd be gone.

36:51.167 --> 36:52.919
I told them we were together in here

36:53.002 --> 36:55.338
so they wouldn't realize
you'd left on your own.

36:56.380 --> 36:58.257
I've been waiting here
for you to get back.

37:04.805 --> 37:07.642
Hah, see? They are here
together just like she said.

37:09.852 --> 37:11.187
I'm going to leave now.

37:11.687 --> 37:14.774
I enjoyed our conversation today.

37:16.150 --> 37:17.360
Oh, yes.

37:17.944 --> 37:18.778
Mm-hmm.

37:19.820 --> 37:20.655
Oh.

37:29.747 --> 37:31.999
What were you doing
in here for four hours?

37:33.417 --> 37:34.335
Good question.

37:35.419 --> 37:36.254
What were…

37:37.338 --> 37:39.006
we doing here for that long?

38:01.362 --> 38:02.780
She must have been bored, huh?

38:07.201 --> 38:09.662
You want to enter
into Songrim's hiring contest?

38:09.745 --> 38:12.290
Yes. Look at what happened today.

38:12.373 --> 38:16.669
Young Master Jang Uk clearly needs me
right by his side at all times.

38:17.545 --> 38:18.462
I have to agree.

38:19.213 --> 38:22.842
How uncomfortable must he have been
to come here to bathe and eat snacks.

38:23.676 --> 38:26.971
Our young master is very sensitive
and was doted on growing up.

38:27.054 --> 38:29.265
So living with others
in Songrim doesn't suit him.

38:29.849 --> 38:31.100
ONE HUNDRED TWENTY-FIVE

38:31.183 --> 38:32.393
I've already put my name in.

38:33.311 --> 38:34.437
I'll get in no matter what.

38:35.438 --> 38:37.315
Yeah, you don't need that.

38:38.024 --> 38:39.525
This is the Jang family.

38:39.608 --> 38:41.068
We can easily put you in there.

38:41.152 --> 38:42.611
Is that true?

38:42.695 --> 38:45.698
So then, does that mean
that I won't have to take the test at all?

38:45.781 --> 38:48.326
Of course not. Just trust me.

38:51.537 --> 38:52.872
That is not possible.

38:53.664 --> 38:57.501
Songrim's servants are only ever chosen
through open recruitments.

38:57.585 --> 38:58.836
There are no exceptions.

38:58.919 --> 39:00.629
Ah, she doesn't need a free post.

39:01.297 --> 39:03.924
Just the entrance plaque.
Just write up her name

39:04.008 --> 39:05.593
so she can have one.

39:05.676 --> 39:07.428
The Jang family will pay her salary.

39:10.973 --> 39:12.058
Also…

39:12.892 --> 39:14.560
here.

39:15.394 --> 39:18.606
I thought it would suit you,
Maidservant Park, so I bought you one.

39:19.190 --> 39:20.024
Huh?

39:23.444 --> 39:24.653
Here.

39:26.280 --> 39:27.323
Hmm.

39:51.013 --> 39:54.683
Word has it that you bribed
Maidservant Park of Songrim

39:55.851 --> 39:57.478
with this simple favor.

39:57.561 --> 40:01.023
- It was not a big deal, just a gift.
- I heard that you asked her

40:02.149 --> 40:04.443
to secure a position there for Mu-deok.

40:04.527 --> 40:07.571
Well, since our young master
is so sensitive,

40:07.655 --> 40:09.573
I thought having Mu-deok close by

40:09.657 --> 40:11.242
would help him improve
his training process,

40:12.034 --> 40:13.661
so I asked her for a favor.

40:15.204 --> 40:16.997
So then, this truly was a bribe!

40:17.790 --> 40:21.085
I apologize. I guess
I wasn't thinking clearly.

40:21.168 --> 40:23.212
When Maidservant Park brought this to me,

40:23.295 --> 40:26.132
I defended you by telling her
you would never actually

40:26.924 --> 40:28.050
do such a thing.

40:28.134 --> 40:32.138
How will I ever dare face
Maidservant Park ever again?

40:32.221 --> 40:33.472
I…

40:35.891 --> 40:36.725
Um…

40:37.852 --> 40:40.020
I will go and apologize to her.

40:40.855 --> 40:42.064
What will everyone think?

40:42.898 --> 40:46.360
They'll definitely think that
you abused your relationship with me

40:46.444 --> 40:48.320
to bribe someone to get what you wanted.

40:48.404 --> 40:51.866
It's true I did give her that scarf,
but I never mentioned your name to her.

40:51.949 --> 40:53.117
Even still,

40:53.200 --> 40:55.828
everyone in Songrim knows
that you and I are close.

40:55.911 --> 40:59.582
If you act like this,
then I can no longer afford…

41:03.085 --> 41:07.006
to continue having
such a close relationship any longer.

41:08.841 --> 41:12.553
Sure! In that case,
I'll just stop coming here.

41:13.888 --> 41:15.931
And besides, maybe our relationship

41:16.015 --> 41:18.642
was never really as deep as
you like to say it was, you know.

41:19.268 --> 41:21.061
Because if we were truly that close,

41:21.145 --> 41:24.190
you would never have mentioned
cutting ties with me so easily, right?

41:24.273 --> 41:25.107
Fine.

41:26.317 --> 41:29.653
- Well, I…
- I'll go to Maidservant Park

41:29.737 --> 41:32.156
and tell her that I, who bribed her,

41:32.239 --> 41:33.657
I am not-- not close at all

41:34.200 --> 41:36.869
with the great leader of Songrim.
I never really had been.

41:36.952 --> 41:38.245
- L-Look, Maidservant--
- Yes…

41:38.829 --> 41:40.289
I'm so terribly sorry

41:40.915 --> 41:42.374
that I embarrassed you this way.

41:43.167 --> 41:44.543
Wait, Maidservant Kim.

41:46.420 --> 41:47.796
You can't just leave like that.

41:55.429 --> 41:56.430
You should take this.

41:58.390 --> 42:01.894
If I were to keep it,
I'd be accepting a bribe.

42:18.786 --> 42:20.246
Also, that is…

42:21.288 --> 42:23.499
You said you'd stop coming.

42:23.999 --> 42:24.833
Um…

42:25.501 --> 42:28.170
that wasn't what I… meant.

42:28.754 --> 42:29.838
Oh, Maid--

42:29.922 --> 42:31.590
Wait! Where are you…

42:36.929 --> 42:38.138
This is hard.

42:56.031 --> 42:57.324
You can't do it yet.

43:00.411 --> 43:01.412
Master Lee.

43:02.079 --> 43:04.915
You can't read that book
with the concentration you have right now.

43:05.666 --> 43:08.836
Because you've never trained
as diligently as the others have.

43:08.919 --> 43:11.922
And how long will it take
if I start my training now?

43:12.548 --> 43:14.425
Well, if you're quick, a year.

43:15.467 --> 43:18.679
I-I cannot do that. I can't spend
a whole year just trapped here.

43:18.762 --> 43:21.890
I think that's exactly the reason
why Park Jin gave you that book.

43:26.562 --> 43:27.896
You could shorten it

43:28.647 --> 43:32.401
if you become my pupil
and receive my tutoring.

43:32.484 --> 43:33.319
You…

43:35.029 --> 43:36.739
mean by drinking the chaste herb tea?

43:39.992 --> 43:42.328
Just give me
a little bit of time to think.

43:43.746 --> 43:46.165
This book, The Words of the Heart

43:46.248 --> 43:50.586
contains a poem written
by my master, Seo Gyeong himself.

43:50.669 --> 43:51.837
Poem?

43:51.920 --> 43:53.756
And it's not that long.

43:54.923 --> 43:57.176
Once you're finally able
to read the first word,

43:57.259 --> 43:59.553
you'll find that the rest comes easily.

44:01.013 --> 44:03.766
Ah, but you can't see it.

44:04.808 --> 44:06.185
Are you having fun teasing me now?

44:06.268 --> 44:07.770
It's not like you're going
to tell me about it.

44:07.853 --> 44:09.146
It's amusing to watch.

44:11.148 --> 44:13.651
Should I help you another time?

44:15.527 --> 44:16.362
Yes.

44:17.279 --> 44:20.532
Let me tell you one secret
about this book that no one knows.

44:21.950 --> 44:23.744
The poem transcribed here is…

44:24.703 --> 44:25.537
a love letter.

44:27.122 --> 44:28.499
A… love letter?

44:28.582 --> 44:29.625
Correct.

44:29.708 --> 44:31.835
Countless mages have been asked
to read this book,

44:31.919 --> 44:33.629
but no one knows it's a love letter.

44:34.546 --> 44:35.673
Ah.

44:37.549 --> 44:41.595
Master Seo Gyeong originally wrote this
for a lady who could not see

44:41.679 --> 44:44.515
so that she would be able
to read it with her heart instead.

44:49.144 --> 44:52.356
You can read it by training
your concentration skills.

44:52.439 --> 44:57.111
But now that you know what it is,
try to think of another way to read it.

44:58.028 --> 45:01.740
How do you think
a love letter is supposed to begin?

45:08.997 --> 45:10.165
What is this thing?

45:13.168 --> 45:14.420
Was he a pervert?

45:14.503 --> 45:18.090
Why would anybody want to
make others read his own love letter, huh?

45:18.590 --> 45:21.301
Oh, why must I read this?
I can't even see it at all.

45:22.136 --> 45:23.429
Was he really a pervert?

45:26.640 --> 45:31.061
Master Lee, it's getting colder.
Instead of returning to Danhyanggok,

45:31.145 --> 45:34.273
why don't you just stay here?
I'll take good care of you.

45:34.356 --> 45:35.649
No.

45:36.150 --> 45:39.027
My training cannot be accomplished
by wearing warm clothes

45:39.111 --> 45:40.863
- and living in comfort.
- Ah.

45:40.946 --> 45:43.323
Master Lee, you know as your pupil,

45:43.407 --> 45:46.618
I just want my master to be warm.

45:48.704 --> 45:51.582
It seems that you've truly matured.

46:08.974 --> 46:12.186
Oh, that's Maidservant Kim
of the Jang family.

46:12.770 --> 46:15.773
Given how unhappy she looks,
she and Jin must have argued.

46:17.357 --> 46:19.151
Oh. Hello.

46:23.739 --> 46:24.948
Master Lee.

46:25.866 --> 46:28.202
Why did you leave so quickly last time?

46:28.285 --> 46:29.995
I didn't even get a chance to thank you.

46:30.078 --> 46:33.290
I take it you two have met before?

46:33.916 --> 46:36.627
That's right. We met
at the celebration at Chwiseonru.

46:36.710 --> 46:37.628
Oh.

46:37.711 --> 46:39.213
I wanted to ask you about your clothes.

46:39.296 --> 46:41.006
Your seam burst because of me.

46:42.800 --> 46:43.842
I'm all right.

46:44.510 --> 46:45.761
What seam?

46:45.844 --> 46:47.137
Ah, I see.

46:47.721 --> 46:48.847
It's very cold out.

46:48.931 --> 46:50.808
Are you not too cold
in those thin clothes?

46:51.809 --> 46:53.602
Why don't you wear this, at least?

46:54.186 --> 46:56.563
I wanted to give you something
to say thank you.

46:59.650 --> 47:02.736
Also, know this is
not a bribe, it's a gift.

47:02.820 --> 47:03.695
Here.

47:22.714 --> 47:23.549
Ah.

47:24.049 --> 47:25.342
It really suits you.

47:34.226 --> 47:35.060
Uh…

47:35.143 --> 47:38.564
are you okay with being warm?

47:47.155 --> 47:51.326
SONGRIM SERVANT CONTEST

47:54.496 --> 47:58.792
We will begin
the Songrim Servant Hiring Contest

47:58.876 --> 48:02.796
to decide on five applicants who
will have the honor to work in Songrim.

48:03.380 --> 48:05.632
I will read the list of applicants.

48:06.341 --> 48:08.594
Answer me when I call your names.

48:11.471 --> 48:13.557
Number one, Park Jun-hwa.

48:13.640 --> 48:14.474
Here.

48:15.100 --> 48:17.019
And two, An So-jeong.

48:17.102 --> 48:18.186
Here!

48:19.980 --> 48:21.064
An So-jeong.

48:21.148 --> 48:22.399
TWO

48:22.482 --> 48:23.483
An…

48:25.152 --> 48:27.487
- Three, Lee Yeong-ok.
- Here.

48:27.571 --> 48:29.865
- Four, Park Hyeon-su.
- Here.

48:30.449 --> 48:32.743
- Five, Bae Hui-young.
- Here.

48:38.624 --> 48:39.458
Huh?

48:40.125 --> 48:41.209
What is this for?

48:41.293 --> 48:42.794
I'm looking just in case.

48:46.590 --> 48:48.926
ONE HUNDRED TWENTY-FIVE, MU-DEOK

48:50.177 --> 48:51.511
There she is.

48:52.012 --> 48:54.890
Number 125. Is Mu-deok here?

48:56.308 --> 48:57.351
Over here!

49:02.522 --> 49:06.443
Your servant, Mu-deok,
is here in Songrim today.

49:07.778 --> 49:09.404
I'm saying this for your sake.

49:09.488 --> 49:10.989
Don't even think of trying to leave here.

49:11.073 --> 49:12.449
Could you please be quiet?

49:15.327 --> 49:16.870
Could you be quiet, please?

49:16.954 --> 49:19.414
I need to concentrate
in order to be able to read this.

49:19.498 --> 49:20.916
I'll let you be then.

49:34.429 --> 49:38.183
Then, I'll see you
in three days, Your Highness.

49:38.266 --> 49:42.104
By the way, why is Songrim
so busy today? Seems crowded.

49:42.854 --> 49:47.192
A contest. They're going to
pick servants for housekeeping today.

49:47.985 --> 49:50.654
- Songrim makes a contest of that?
- Your Highness.

49:51.238 --> 49:53.532
Being a Songrim's servant
is a coveted position.

49:53.615 --> 49:54.449
When I looked,

49:54.533 --> 49:56.743
I saw the Jang family's servant there,
Your Highness.

49:58.120 --> 50:00.205
- Filthy Mu-deok?
- Yes, sire.

50:13.593 --> 50:15.137
The first test you'll face

50:15.721 --> 50:20.267
will test the strength
of your reading and arithmetic skills.

50:21.059 --> 50:22.769
You'll have to get full marks to pass.

50:22.853 --> 50:25.522
Get just one question wrong,
and you're disqualified!

50:29.109 --> 50:30.944
SONGRIM SERVANT CONTEST

50:33.780 --> 50:35.615
Yul! Yul!

50:38.118 --> 50:38.994
I found the test.

50:41.371 --> 50:43.874
So many questions. Even writing.

50:44.583 --> 50:47.252
Mu-deok is smart,
but can she answer them all?

50:50.797 --> 50:51.757
This is pretty hard.

50:52.257 --> 50:55.052
Eunuch Oh, what do you use
to wash clothes stained with ink?

50:55.135 --> 50:56.178
That's a question.

50:56.261 --> 50:58.722
For ink-stained clothes,
rice paste does the trick.

50:59.347 --> 51:00.599
What do you do with it?

51:00.682 --> 51:03.518
Well, first, you apply it
to the stain, and then you can…

51:08.482 --> 51:09.316
SONGRIM SERVANT CONTEST

51:09.399 --> 51:12.736
"You have invited
20 guests each from 3 different families."

51:12.819 --> 51:16.198
"One table seats four people.
How many tables do you need to provide?"

51:18.075 --> 51:21.620
Twenty people from
three families, 60 total.

51:23.705 --> 51:27.125
Each table can fit four people,

51:28.210 --> 51:30.295
- so it's fifteen.
- No, no, no.

51:30.378 --> 51:32.422
They said "three families" on purpose.

51:33.340 --> 51:37.385
Each family must push
their tables together.

51:38.095 --> 51:40.430
We need more tables
if they're pushed together.

51:40.514 --> 51:42.808
Each family needs nine tables.

51:44.101 --> 51:45.143
NINE × THREE = TWENTY-SEVEN

51:45.227 --> 51:48.522
- So, 27.
- Ooh, ooh, ooh, ooh. Ooh!

51:52.067 --> 51:53.193
It said they're invited.

51:53.693 --> 51:55.153
NINE × THREE = TWENTY-SEVEN

51:55.237 --> 51:57.656
That means the host
will require a table as well.

51:58.657 --> 52:00.200
TWENTY-SEVEN + HOST = TWENTY…

52:00.283 --> 52:01.785
Twenty-eight total.

52:04.204 --> 52:06.081
Ooh, you're right,
you're right, you're right.

52:06.998 --> 52:09.000
TWENTY-EIGHT

52:09.501 --> 52:12.254
The next one's about knowing the streets
well enough to run errands.

52:13.046 --> 52:15.423
I'll… go try to find a map.

52:16.675 --> 52:18.844
HOW DO YOU WASH CLOTHES
THAT HAVE INK ON THEM?

52:19.511 --> 52:21.805
How should you wash clothes
with ink on them again?

52:21.888 --> 52:24.516
Shouldn't you just discard them?
Hey, Eunuch Oh.

52:25.559 --> 52:26.685
Your Highness.

52:26.768 --> 52:29.771
How are you supposed to wash clothes
that have been stained with ink again?

52:29.855 --> 52:31.940
For ink-stained clothes,
you need some hot rice paste.

52:32.023 --> 52:33.900
- First, you smear it on the--
- Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah, that's it.

52:33.984 --> 52:34.943
Oh!

52:35.026 --> 52:36.027
Write it.

52:37.028 --> 52:38.613
Hot rice paste.

52:39.906 --> 52:41.741
SONGRIM SERVANT CONTEST

52:43.618 --> 52:44.911
I'm sure we got them all right.

52:45.412 --> 52:47.539
This was unexpected but interesting.

52:48.165 --> 52:50.500
And I am sure that Mu-deok will fail it.

52:53.712 --> 52:54.546
Uh…

52:54.629 --> 52:56.840
yeah, maybe we should probably find a way

52:56.923 --> 52:59.301
to deliver this perfect test sheet
to her right now.

53:00.802 --> 53:04.055
But how should we do it?
It'll look too obvious if we go.

53:05.307 --> 53:09.603
Perhaps if it's someone more conspicuous,
they won't be scrutinized as much.

53:19.571 --> 53:20.530
Hmm?

53:25.493 --> 53:28.163
SONGRIM SERVANT CONTEST

53:29.497 --> 53:30.415
This is hard.

53:31.333 --> 53:33.084
It's much harder than I thought.

53:35.128 --> 53:36.922
Hey, do not look at other people's papers.

53:40.300 --> 53:43.720
The Crown Prince is here!
Bow before him!

53:46.431 --> 53:48.642
- Bow before him!
- Oh. Your Royal Highness!

53:57.817 --> 54:01.154
I heard there's a test.
I thought I'd offer some encouragement.

54:03.198 --> 54:04.741
We are honored, sire.

54:04.824 --> 54:07.911
Do not mind me.
Focus on your test.

54:25.929 --> 54:26.846
Go back to work.

54:28.306 --> 54:29.349
Focus!

54:30.225 --> 54:31.434
Back to work.

54:31.518 --> 54:32.769
- And you too.
- Back--

54:33.395 --> 54:34.562
Go on and focus on something.

55:16.479 --> 55:18.565
I will now announce those of you

55:18.648 --> 55:20.692
who have passed the written test.

55:23.486 --> 55:26.364
Park Jun-hwa has passed.

55:27.157 --> 55:29.367
Lee Yeong-ok, failed.

55:29.451 --> 55:32.537
Hwang Yeon-ji, failed.

55:33.371 --> 55:35.165
Oh Jae-ho, passed.

55:38.001 --> 55:39.586
Number 125.

55:39.669 --> 55:41.004
Mu-deok.

55:50.972 --> 55:52.390
Your Royal Highness!

55:54.726 --> 55:56.186
She passed it.

55:56.269 --> 55:57.812
Yes! Oh, yes!

55:57.896 --> 55:59.814
All right! Yeah!

56:02.067 --> 56:02.901
Good work.

56:04.110 --> 56:07.864
Forty of you have passed the written test.

56:08.365 --> 56:11.868
We shall now begin the practical.

56:14.454 --> 56:18.625
The practical test evaluates them on
their ability to carry out their duties.

56:19.626 --> 56:20.960
They'll prepare ingredients,

56:21.044 --> 56:23.880
clean, in addition to
washing dirty laundry.

56:23.963 --> 56:26.424
And last but not least,
they'll do a fitness test.

56:55.745 --> 56:58.373
Number 125, Mu-deok.

56:58.456 --> 56:59.416
You passed.

57:27.527 --> 57:28.361
Oh!

57:28.903 --> 57:30.989
Number 125, Mu-deok.

57:31.072 --> 57:32.407
You passed!

57:46.588 --> 57:48.882
Number 125, Mu-deok.

57:49.382 --> 57:50.717
You passed!

57:54.012 --> 57:56.556
Wow, Mu-deok is so impressive.

57:56.639 --> 57:58.433
There's only the fitness test left.

57:58.516 --> 58:00.018
We should go and cheer for her, right?

58:01.186 --> 58:04.105
I saw many fit individuals back there.

58:04.189 --> 58:06.441
I highly doubt that
she'll be in the top five.

58:06.524 --> 58:08.776
Sire, thank you for all of your help.

58:09.360 --> 58:10.320
Goodbye.

58:12.614 --> 58:14.741
- Let's go.
- Yeah, let's go.

58:17.285 --> 58:21.206
That was his way
of telling me not to come, right?

58:21.289 --> 58:23.708
Oh, goodness, why are they being so mean?

58:23.791 --> 58:25.293
Unbelievable!

58:26.920 --> 58:28.421
Whatever. Let us go.

58:29.297 --> 58:30.507
It is this way, Your Highness.

58:33.510 --> 58:35.345
- Yeah, I knew that. I did.
- Of course.

58:36.513 --> 58:39.390
From here,
you will travel five ri

58:39.474 --> 58:40.934
and bring back water.

58:41.017 --> 58:41.851
The winners…

58:43.144 --> 58:46.439
have to be the first five
to return with water.

58:47.690 --> 58:48.942
This is the last hurdle.

58:50.151 --> 58:51.819
I must be in the first five.

59:04.332 --> 59:05.917
Begin.

59:13.883 --> 59:15.468
He has not moved, he's just been staring

59:15.552 --> 59:16.886
at the book for days on end.

59:18.638 --> 59:19.514
Really?

59:28.022 --> 59:30.024
It can't be achieved overnight.

59:30.108 --> 59:31.568
You must have patience.

59:33.778 --> 59:34.612
Yes.

59:35.780 --> 59:39.075
Maidservant Kim is worried sick about you.

59:39.951 --> 59:41.744
Let me know if you need anything.

59:41.828 --> 59:45.999
I can prepare your bed, your food,
and clothing to your liking.

59:47.834 --> 59:49.252
I'll be all right.

59:58.511 --> 01:00:00.763
The wind is getting colder.

01:00:00.847 --> 01:00:02.849
Keep the windows closed.

01:00:04.934 --> 01:00:08.980
Master Seo Gyeong originally wrote this
for a lady who could not see

01:00:09.063 --> 01:00:12.025
so that she would be able
to read it with her heart instead.

01:00:13.651 --> 01:00:14.944
I have one question.

01:00:16.362 --> 01:00:20.241
Did Master Seo Gyeong use to know
a woman who couldn't see?

01:00:24.203 --> 01:00:26.497
In the Great Chaos, centuries ago,

01:00:27.165 --> 01:00:29.417
the woman who stood
at Master Seo Gyeong's side

01:00:29.500 --> 01:00:31.878
was the very first leader of Jinyowon.

01:00:31.961 --> 01:00:34.922
And she was unable to see anything.

01:00:36.215 --> 01:00:38.134
So the recipient of this love letter

01:00:38.217 --> 01:00:39.636
was the leader of Jinyowon.

01:00:41.763 --> 01:00:45.850
Are you sure that it's all right
if other people read this letter?

01:00:46.601 --> 01:00:48.645
What if these details
are his private life,

01:00:48.728 --> 01:00:50.813
and you're just requiring
everybody to read them?

01:00:52.523 --> 01:00:53.358
Hmm.

01:00:54.984 --> 01:00:57.862
You must be trying to use me
to figure out what is written in there.

01:00:58.529 --> 01:00:59.614
I will tell you this.

01:01:00.406 --> 01:01:05.453
Nothing written here is secret
or even at all something personal.

01:01:07.705 --> 01:01:09.916
Countless mages have been asked
to read this book,

01:01:09.999 --> 01:01:12.251
but no one knows it's a love letter.

01:01:12.835 --> 01:01:15.672
Right. He said that
no one knows it's a love letter.

01:01:15.755 --> 01:01:17.715
Instead of coming up with tricks,

01:01:17.799 --> 01:01:20.259
concentrate on training yourself.

01:01:21.052 --> 01:01:24.263
If it's a love letter,
how is it that no one knows?

01:01:29.310 --> 01:01:32.063
You can read it by training
your concentration skills.

01:01:32.605 --> 01:01:37.193
But now that you know what it is,
try to think of another way to read it.

01:01:38.027 --> 01:01:39.654
There must be
a different way to read it

01:01:39.737 --> 01:01:41.698
when you know that it's a love letter.

01:01:42.740 --> 01:01:44.909
A way those in training don't know.

01:01:44.992 --> 01:01:47.495
But those who know
it's a love letter can see.

01:01:48.079 --> 01:01:48.996
What could it be?

01:01:49.622 --> 01:01:52.709
How do you think
a love letter is supposed to begin?

01:02:03.761 --> 01:02:05.138
I have one last question.

01:02:06.139 --> 01:02:07.557
The first leader of Jinyowon,

01:02:08.808 --> 01:02:10.059
tell me what was her name.

01:02:22.905 --> 01:02:24.449
Love letters must always…

01:02:26.033 --> 01:02:27.910
begin with the name of the recipient.

01:02:28.828 --> 01:02:29.954
Her name?

01:02:30.037 --> 01:02:33.708
Her surname was Jin,
and given name Seol-ran.

01:02:34.208 --> 01:02:37.044
The recipient's name was Jin Seol-ran.

01:02:37.128 --> 01:02:38.546
A blue orchid that blooms

01:02:39.922 --> 01:02:41.132
in white snow.

01:02:42.800 --> 01:02:43.885
Her name will…

01:02:45.219 --> 01:02:47.096
help reveal this letter's context.

01:03:25.593 --> 01:03:26.427
That's it.

01:03:34.977 --> 01:03:36.979
Hey, hey, hey, Yul, look!

01:03:38.981 --> 01:03:40.608
There she goes, Mu-deok.

01:03:55.289 --> 01:03:56.707
"You cannot grasp water,

01:03:58.209 --> 01:03:59.544
but it's within the soil."

01:04:01.546 --> 01:04:02.922
"You cannot touch fire,

01:04:03.673 --> 01:04:04.966
but it is within the tree."

01:04:07.426 --> 01:04:08.928
"You cannot hold the wind…

01:04:10.930 --> 01:04:12.181
but it rests on the rock."

01:04:14.100 --> 01:04:17.728
"If you let them be,
they will be everywhere."

01:04:19.647 --> 01:04:21.649
"The faint, blue light

01:04:22.733 --> 01:04:24.068
makes me sigh."

01:04:26.904 --> 01:04:28.239
"My white breath

01:04:29.657 --> 01:04:31.868
turns into snow and gathers like tears."

01:04:32.994 --> 01:04:35.788
"So I cannot drop it but hide it away."

01:04:37.373 --> 01:04:39.876
"Despite knowing that
they will well up once again,

01:04:40.835 --> 01:04:45.131
"I am a fool
who dares not shed a single tear."

01:04:50.469 --> 01:04:52.096
There are two back already.

01:04:54.724 --> 01:04:55.933
I don't see Mu-deok.

01:05:04.525 --> 01:05:05.985
There are six people
ahead of her.

01:05:06.694 --> 01:05:08.905
She needs to overtake
at least two of them to win.

01:05:19.373 --> 01:05:22.460
I AM A FOOL
WHO DARES NOT SHED A SINGLE TEAR

01:05:29.759 --> 01:05:31.969
YOU CANNOT GRASP WATER
BUT IT IS INSIDE THE SOIL

01:05:38.601 --> 01:05:39.685
Where are you going?

01:05:40.728 --> 01:05:41.562
Oh.

01:05:44.357 --> 01:05:45.441
I finished reading it.

01:06:07.880 --> 01:06:10.841
Number 29, Jang Jeong-do. You passed.

01:06:11.842 --> 01:06:14.053
And now, only one more remains.

01:06:47.044 --> 01:06:49.130
I have no need
for a pupil who won't improve.

01:06:49.630 --> 01:06:51.716
If you're not going to do
anything, you should just die.

01:06:52.758 --> 01:06:54.760
Stop that! Damn! You just threw it.

01:06:54.844 --> 01:06:56.554
Don't act like you're still Naksu, okay?

01:07:03.394 --> 01:07:05.187
No matter how pathetic I feel,

01:07:06.272 --> 01:07:08.357
I must do what I can right now.

01:07:10.818 --> 01:07:12.695
If I am not willing to do anything,

01:07:14.280 --> 01:07:15.740
I might as well die.

01:07:35.217 --> 01:07:37.094
Number 125, Mu-deok.

01:07:39.513 --> 01:07:40.848
You passed!

01:07:48.397 --> 01:07:49.982
YOU CANNOT GRASP WATER
BUT IT IS INSIDE THE SOIL

01:07:50.066 --> 01:07:52.777
It's word for word what is written
in the Words of the Heart.

01:07:53.569 --> 01:07:55.488
Jang Uk has done it.

01:07:57.907 --> 01:07:59.366
Jang Uk has done it?

01:08:04.205 --> 01:08:05.456
Where is he right now?

01:08:06.248 --> 01:08:07.374
He's at Sejukwon.

01:08:07.458 --> 01:08:10.753
The servant who was always with him
collapsed during the test,

01:08:10.836 --> 01:08:12.046
so he took her there, sir.

01:08:13.214 --> 01:08:14.048
His servant?

01:08:15.049 --> 01:08:17.009
- You mean his servant, Mu-deok?
- Yes.

01:08:17.093 --> 01:08:19.053
She was one of five
who passed the test today.

01:08:19.762 --> 01:08:21.972
She did faint as soon as
she reached the finish line,

01:08:22.056 --> 01:08:24.100
but still she-- she has made it.

01:08:24.809 --> 01:08:25.643
Really?

01:08:30.356 --> 01:08:33.692
All she did was risk her life
following the orders I gave.

01:08:34.401 --> 01:08:36.362
It was all because of me, sir.

01:08:48.791 --> 01:08:49.792
Now, I think…

01:08:51.877 --> 01:08:54.046
she was always at Uk's side.

01:08:56.090 --> 01:08:57.508
His servant, Mu-deok.

01:09:03.597 --> 01:09:07.226
The book was actually
Master Seo Gyeong's love letter.

01:09:10.104 --> 01:09:10.938
Really?

01:09:12.189 --> 01:09:14.275
Then why did he choose
to make it invisible?

01:09:15.025 --> 01:09:18.612
The woman he loved was blind.
He wanted her to read it with her heart.

01:09:20.114 --> 01:09:21.448
That's so sweet.

01:09:22.032 --> 01:09:22.867
I don't think

01:09:23.909 --> 01:09:25.828
the letter actually reached her
in the end, though.

01:09:26.495 --> 01:09:28.455
If it had, it would be in Jinyowon,

01:09:29.331 --> 01:09:30.916
instead of being here at Songrim.

01:09:31.500 --> 01:09:34.670
A love letter that can't be seen
and was never sent?

01:09:36.797 --> 01:09:37.882
What a coward!

01:09:39.842 --> 01:09:42.178
He just wrote his feelings
and never told her.

01:09:43.679 --> 01:09:44.763
What a foolish…

01:09:46.390 --> 01:09:47.933
pitiful love letter.

01:09:53.564 --> 01:09:55.482
You're right. Love letters should be…

01:09:58.569 --> 01:10:00.404
delivered to the recipients like this.

01:10:01.864 --> 01:10:04.491
RECRUITING SERVANTS FOR SONGRIM

01:10:05.993 --> 01:10:07.328
That isn't a letter, though.

01:10:07.411 --> 01:10:08.746
And what is a letter?

01:10:08.829 --> 01:10:11.582
As long as it reveals your heart,
then it's a letter.

01:10:13.125 --> 01:10:15.628
Just wait there.
I'll be there soon, too.

01:10:15.711 --> 01:10:17.463
Be safe. Don't get caught.

01:10:26.847 --> 01:10:31.435
You must have felt
sorry for me… taking that exam.

01:10:32.019 --> 01:10:34.647
You were once
an incredibly powerful mage, so…

01:10:35.147 --> 01:10:36.857
of course, I did feel sorry for you.

01:10:37.900 --> 01:10:40.402
I suppose I taught you
something about loyalty.

01:10:40.486 --> 01:10:42.529
Seeing how far my master would go,

01:10:42.613 --> 01:10:45.991
I did think that I should be doing
my very best as your pupil.

01:10:48.285 --> 01:10:49.495
You must have felt pressured.

01:10:49.578 --> 01:10:51.705
Hmm. No, I didn't really.

01:10:52.373 --> 01:10:53.499
But I was conflicted

01:10:54.375 --> 01:10:57.169
if I should answer this letter
as your young master

01:10:57.253 --> 01:10:59.129
or if I should answer as your pupil,

01:10:59.713 --> 01:11:02.383
or just answer based on what I read.

01:11:08.305 --> 01:11:09.682
Well, what did you read?

01:11:10.766 --> 01:11:14.478
Should I answer
based on that, you think, also?

01:11:16.188 --> 01:11:17.606
Also? What?

01:11:18.190 --> 01:11:19.692
It's written right here.

01:11:19.775 --> 01:11:22.361
"This is how far I will go
just to be able to see you."

01:11:23.028 --> 01:11:26.323
"I'll do absolutely anything
if I can just see you."

01:11:26.949 --> 01:11:28.242
And this is my answer to that.

01:11:33.455 --> 01:11:37.918
I should have braced myself
before letting someone get this close.

01:11:42.047 --> 01:11:43.382
I missed you, too. A lot.

01:11:47.511 --> 01:11:48.679
That's my response.

01:11:58.063 --> 01:11:59.273
What I gave him…

01:12:01.317 --> 01:12:05.321
should not have been read
or even delivered.

01:12:07.323 --> 01:12:08.824
My foolish and pitiful…

01:12:10.617 --> 01:12:11.702
love letter.

01:12:43.609 --> 01:12:45.235
I miss you when I open my eyes.

01:12:45.319 --> 01:12:47.237
- I miss you every second they're open.
- Stop that.

01:12:47.321 --> 01:12:49.406
It seems that
you've already taken the poison.

01:12:49.490 --> 01:12:51.450
The antidote is
the person who poisons you.

01:12:51.533 --> 01:12:52.910
Are you out of your damn mind?

01:12:52.993 --> 01:12:54.870
It's just another symptom. I was poisoned?

01:12:54.953 --> 01:12:58.082
So the only one in your mind
has been Jang Uk, Naksu.

01:12:58.165 --> 01:13:00.292
It's not like you really believe
that I'm in love with you.

01:13:00.376 --> 01:13:02.336
Then do a better job
and make me believe it.

01:13:02.419 --> 01:13:04.880
That is the most precious thing
I've ever owned in my life.

01:13:04.963 --> 01:13:07.883
Please, try to win just once.
And win it back for me.

01:13:07.966 --> 01:13:10.761
Well, you see, I made a bet.
I made a bet with your servant there.

01:13:10.844 --> 01:13:13.055
Fight and perish, Jang Uk.

01:13:13.138 --> 01:13:14.223
So this is what you meant that day

01:13:14.306 --> 01:13:15.724
when you told me that you had my weakness?

01:13:15.808 --> 01:13:17.142
Stop!

01:13:17.810 --> 01:13:21.438
I… I missed you too, a lot.
